From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0310: XMA cross-buffer packet resolution

Source: $IOS tools/parche_xma_paquetes.py, rebased onto Renan's rexglue-xma-decoder-fixes by W0.3; code shape from
  Xenia Canary src/xenia/apu/xma_context_new.cc (its own header kept below)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); code shape from Xenia Canary (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2024 Xenia
  Canary)
Purpose: XMA: a packet skip that runs past the end of the current input buffer resolves to packet (index - count) of
  the other buffer, not that buffer's first packet. Cvar xma_cross_buffer_packets (default true; false = SDK
  behaviour). Not built before G1: A/B it on the first audio test.
Bucket: PORT

0310-xma-cross-buffer-packets.patch (mcla-x86 W0.3 rebase of $IOS/tools/parche_xma_paquetes.py onto Renan's
rexglue-xma-decoder-fixes.patch; code shape from Xenia Canary src/xenia/apu/xma_context_new.cc GetPacketHandle /
GetNextPacket / GetNextPacketReadOffset(data, ...), BSD-3-Clause, "Copyright 2024 Xenia Canary")

Purpose. Each XMA context has two input buffers. A packet's skip count can run past the end of the current one;
the packet it names is then packet (index - packets left) of the OTHER buffer. ReXGlue v0.10.0 (and Renan's
patched decoder) returns that buffer's FIRST packet instead, and when the read offset moves on it takes the other
buffer's first frame, so on every such crossing the wrong packet is decoded. Renan's xma_canary_fixes took the
skip-chain half of the Canary delta (7015473a7) but not this one; Canary canary_experimental still has it.

Change. Cvar xma_cross_buffer_packets (Audio, default true, sampled per Work() like xma_canary_fixes; false = the
SDK's behaviour). PacketHandle + GetPacketHandle(data, index, count) resolve (buffer, index); GetNextPacket and a
new GetNextPacketReadOffset(data, ...) use it; Decode's full-skip (0xFF) and last-frame paths swap to the other
buffer when the next packet is there and keep the offset computed in it. Not taken from parche_xma_paquetes: its
diagnostics. Syntax-checked only (clang 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only); not built or run. Verify on the first audio test
(radio pair, police chatter) with the cvar on and off.

---
diff --git a/include/rex/audio/xma/context.h b/include/rex/audio/xma/context.h
